# Cubic SrTiO3, written the way Rietveld programs often write it: element
# symbols with no charges, so Eir has to be told the oxidation states
# (eir check SrTiO3_refined.cif --ox Sr=2,Ti=4,O=-2).
# A constructed example for Eir, not a deposited structure; the lattice
# parameter is the standard room-temperature value.
data_SrTiO3_example
_audit_creation_method 'Constructed for the Eir examples'
_chemical_formula_sum 'O3 Sr Ti'
_cell_length_a 3.9050(1)
_cell_length_b 3.9050(1)
_cell_length_c 3.9050(1)
_cell_angle_alpha 90
_cell_angle_beta 90
_cell_angle_gamma 90
_space_group_name_H-M_alt 'P m -3 m'
_space_group_IT_number 221
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
_atom_site_occupancy
_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv
Sr1 Sr 0.5 0.5 0.5 1 0.0060(2)
Ti1 Ti 0 0 0 1 0.0040(2)
O1 O 0.5 0 0 1 0.0080(3)
